Z||000005||Monkeyman||01-14-2000||04:43 AM||||Didn't we decide in an earlier thread that putting scoops over the grilles would make the engine compartment hotter?  No way for the air to escape?  I posted a pic of a car just like that (maybe the same one from a different angle?).  Looks racy, but if you do that maybe you should buy a reversed hood scoop like Tom sells as well.  Just my unknowledgeable (must not be spelled correctly-too many letters <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) mind at work.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||01-14-2000||05:56 AM||||You're right Monkeyman. I had a set of those scoops on my coupe back in 95 and didn't know at the time that it disrupts the natural air flow for the engine. Then you got to think whats going on back there when your stuck in traffic!! Yes, they look great, but a real "functional" scoop system to me would be Tom's trunk scoop with scooped quarter windows(if you have a GT)and a set of Mecham or original side scoops. I have the first two and will get the Mechams for my birthday in April! ||||reg||2
